kunzite: Adreno 710, glue plan K5's R2 part (main repo ios/gpu-glue-plan.md 3.2, 4): RedwoodGPU's
buffers and imported surfaces in translated mode. Buffers are write-combined by default, as Linux's
msm gives freedreno: no buffer of the program's is pushed out of the cache at each submission (on
#55: 25 MB pushed for 7 submissions, about 1 ms each), and what the GPU writes the CPU reads without
invalidating;
gpu_cached=1 keeps the old cached buffers. Topaz's note that a write-combined IOBMD comes out
contiguous from the lower DDR bank does not hold for this tree's IOBufferMemoryDescriptor. A new
buffer is pushed out of the cache once at creation in both modes (dc civac through its alias), so
no dirty zero line from the allocator is written back over it later. Client-memory surfaces carry
wrapDelta: mapped for wrapDelta + allocSize, with the delta in the offset reported (the GPU saw
the picture wrapDelta bytes early and its end unmapped); refused when longer than the descriptor.
Client memory the task could only read (the read-only fallback of sweet_surface_use_task_memory)
is mapped for the GPU read-only (MSM_BO_GPU_READONLY). Identity mode is unchanged.

